      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Moving to hardware keys like YubiKeys shifts your security baseline to Tier 1 help, effectively neutralizing SIM swap attacks and SMS interception. While threat actors still target other weak links, hardware keys survive remote attacks because they require physical possession and often还记得 a device binding that makes them impervious to phishing attempts common with SMS. This drastically reduces the \"attack surface\" compared to SMS, though it does not create an impregnable fortress against social engineering if the employee themselves is compromised physically.",
